From: Nura rc4t venus series <rc4t-venus@nura.invalid>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 11:19:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: guacamole: enable the Venus video codec

Turn the SoC's video-codec node on for the OnePlus 7 Pro and point it at
the board's firmware.

There is no SM8150 Venus firmware in linux-firmware. The board's copy is
the split venus.mdt + venus.b00-b04 set in the NON-HLOS modem partition
(::/image, VIDEO.IR.1.2-00035). This optional set ships it in the kernel
package as /usr/lib/firmware/qcom/sm8150/oneplus7/venus.mdt, next to the
other remoteproc firmware. Its load span is 0x4ff020 bytes, which fits
the 5 MiB venus_mem region that sm8150-oneplus-common.dtsi places at
0x97200000.

The SoC node, its OPP table and the driver support come from the SM8150
Venus series of the AOSPA raphael tree (snowf14k3), backported to 7.0.

Nura-Category: device-dt
Nura-Origin: nura rc4t venus optional set (experimental)
Upstream-Status: WIP
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-guacamole-nura.dtsi   | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-guacamole-nura.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-guacamole-nura.dtsi
index 559bc98a6..ced8508c2 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-guacamole-nura.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-guacamole-nura.dtsi
@@ -719,3 +719,14 @@ nfc: nfc@28 {
 			    <&nfc_clk_req_default>;
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * Venus video codec (IRIS1), experimental optional set (flows/rc4/optional/venus).
+ * The firmware is the board's own split copy from the NON-HLOS modem
+ * partition, shipped in the kernel package next to the modem, ADSP and
+ * SLPI firmware.
+ */
+&venus {
+	firmware-name = "qcom/sm8150/oneplus7/venus.mdt";
+	status = "okay";
+};
